    "svg": "architecture.svg",
    "medium": "documentation and notebook",
    "alt_text": "A modern MCP host receives untrusted discovery metadata and a model call proposal. Trusted inventory reconciles authenticated connection identity with an exact catalog contract, then application policy validates identity, token audience, scope, tenant, confirmation, and current state before issuing a one-use execution grant. The official MCP client invokes a server with a narrow downstream capability. Server-produced results pass through a schema, tenant, resource, error, and size gate before entering model context with an untrusted-content label. Privacy-minimized receipts record every decision phase."
